t engages in the generation, distribution, and transmission of electricity to approximately 2.8 million residential, commercial, industrial, and governmental customers in Virginia and North Carolina. The Dominion Energy South Carolina segment generates, transmits, and distributes electricity to approximately 0.8 million customers in the central, southern, and southwestern portions of South Carolina; and distributes natural gas to approximately 0.5 million residential, commercial, and industrial customers in South Carolina. The Contracted Energy segment is involved in the nonregulated long-term contracted renewable electric generation fleet and renewable natural gas facilities. As of December 31, 2025, the company's portfolio of assets included approximately 30.7 GW of electric generating capacity, 10,800 miles of electric transmission lines, and 80,400 miles of electric distribution lines. The company was formerly known as Dominion Resources, Inc. Dominion Energy, Inc. was incorporated in 1983 and is headquartered in Richmond, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert M. Blue | President, CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 57 | Compensation: $5.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 15K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Dominion Energy, Inc. is a large-cap utilities business with a $59.5B market cap on $16.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $7.3B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.3%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Price sits 27% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2708539968604364},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 88% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"amber","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Utilities peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["41 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Dominion Energy Inc. (D) \u2013 What Are Investment Firms Thinking About This Stock?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/dominion-energy-inc-d-what-are-investment-firms-thinking-about-this-stock.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794394070.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.827,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Dominion (NYSE:D) Sweetening Its Data Center Terms?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/utility/is-dominion-nysed-sweetening-its-data-center-terms","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794378960.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.727,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"2% Undervalued? Dominion Energy (D) After Earnings Guidance And New Bond Deals","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-d/dominion-energy/news/2-undervalued-dominion-energy-d-after-earnings-guidance-and","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794201638.079,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.743,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Dominion Energy Charitable Foundation Awards $4.5 million in Grants to Nonprofit Organizations Across Multiple States","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/dominion-energy-charitable-foundation-awards-150000097.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794582000.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.944,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Much You Need in Southern, Dominion and AEP to Collect $1,000 a Month","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/much-southern-dominion-aep-collect-171724000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794590782.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.153,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"People Pay the Power Bill Before Almost Anything Else. $45,000 in Each of These 3 Utilities Pays $5,915 a Year","source":"aol.com","link":"https://ww